    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "STRING BASICS\n\nText is a String. The String nodes are pure: they take text in and give text (or a number / boolean)\nback, never changing the original. Each step below reads a variable, applies one node and stores the\nanswer in another variable so you can follow it:\n  text = \"  Hello, Pulsar!  \"  ->  Trim -> Uppercase / Lowercase / Length / Contains / Replace ...",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          190.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "READING THE GRAPH\nBegin Play runs nine Set nodes in a row. Under each node the variable it reads is shown as a Get node. Expected: trimmed \"Hello, Pulsar!\", shout \"HELLO, PULSAR!\", whisper \"hello, pulsar!\", length 14, contains true, starts-with true, replaced \"Hello, World!\", first word \"Hello\" (characters 0..5), mirrored \"!rasluP ,olleH\".",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -70.0
        ],
        "size": [
